;
; Does the classic chipset display driver come up, and can the guest read what
; Denise drew?
;
; Two independent claims, and they fail differently.
;
; AmigaVideo in DEVS:Monitors is run by AROSMonDrvs before this point; if it
; registered, graphics.library has a second display driver and a second
; monitor. Version reports whether the library is there at all.
;
; DeniseView reads the frame aperture Bellatrix publishes at $01000000. Its
; census is meant to be compared with the one Bellatrix prints on its own side:
; same background, same count, same checksum means the frame the chipset
; composed is the frame the guest can see.
;
; NOWINDOW because this runs from the Startup-Sequence with nothing to display
; on yet, and because the claim being tested is readability, not presentation.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[denise-view] --- display drivers on the card"
List >DEBUG: DEVS:Drivers/amigavideo.hidd DEVS:Drivers/vcgfx.hidd
List >DEBUG: DEVS:Monitors/AmigaVideo DEVS:Monitors/VideoCore

Echo >DEBUG: "[denise-view] --- did amigavideo.hidd load?"
Version >DEBUG: amigavideo.hidd

Echo >DEBUG: "[denise-view] --- reading the frame aperture"
DeniseView >DEBUG: NOWINDOW
Echo >DEBUG: "[denise-view] --- done"
